{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791651119,"nonce":"iroj1qhvgYGxzpnzy+uFUrTxKgc=","title":"text_input draws no caret after the in-place rebuild","message":"Since b4fa30772178cc0a1bf024106d39b01f07b7c43e (dba8d31) a focused text input shows no caret.\n\nThe caret canvas decides when to draw from the field's data (focused, nothing selected), then takes its blink opacity from `CursorState::current_opacity`, which returns 0 unless `CursorState::visible` is set. Only the old per-state rebuild set `visible`; the field is now built once, so nothing sets it and the caret paints nothing.\n\nFix: `CursorState::blink_opacity`, the blink without the `visible` gate, for a caret whose owner decides when it shows. `current_opacity` is the gate plus that. text_area and the code editor still set `visible` and keep using `current_opacity`.\n\nThe in-place tests checked text, look, scroll and selection runs but never painted the caret canvas. `the_caret_shows_while_focused_with_nothing_selected` now paints it into a `RecordingContext`; it fails with the old opacity call.","files":null}]}